---
title: PipeWire
order: 1
description: PipeWire audio server, WirePlumber, and pw-cli tools
tags: [audio, pipewire, pw-cli, pw-top, pw-dump, pw-record, wireplumber, wpctl]
---

PipeWire is the modern audio/video server replacing PulseAudio and JACK.
WirePlumber is its session manager handling device routing and policy.

@code bash
# Install PipeWire stack
sudo pacman -S pipewire pipewire-pulse pipewire-alsa pipewire-jack wireplumber

# Start PipeWire (user service via pipewire-launcher or XDG autostart)
# On Artix without systemd, PipeWire typically starts via:
# - XDG autostart desktop entries
# - KDE Plasma session startup
# - Manual: pipewire & pipewire-pulse & wireplumber &

# Check if PipeWire is running
pw-cli info 0                    # query the core object (ID 0)
pactl info | grep "Server Name"  # should show PipeWire

@text
wpctl is the primary tool for managing audio devices and volumes
through WirePlumber.

@code bash
# List all audio devices and streams
wpctl status

# Get/set volume (ID from wpctl status, or use @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@)
wpctl get-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@
wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 0.5        # set to 50%
wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 5%+        # increase by 5%
wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 5%-        # decrease by 5%
wpctl set-volume -l 1.0 @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 10%+  # cap at 100%

# Mute/unmute
wpctl set-mute @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ toggle
wpctl set-mute @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 1            # mute
wpctl set-mute @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 0            # unmute

# Set default sink/source
wpctl set-default <id>           # ID from wpctl status

# Inspect a node
wpctl inspect <id>

@text
pw-cli provides low-level control over PipeWire objects.

@code bash
# List all objects
pw-cli list-objects

# Detailed info about an object
pw-cli info <id>
pw-cli info all                  # everything

# Enumerate specific types
pw-cli enum-params <id> Props    # object properties
pw-cli enum-params <id> Format   # supported formats

# Create a link between ports
pw-link <output-port> <input-port>
pw-link -o                       # list output ports
pw-link -i                       # list input ports
pw-link -l                       # list existing links
pw-link -d <output-port> <input-port>  # disconnect

@text
Monitoring and debugging PipeWire.

@code bash
# Real-time performance monitor
pw-top                           # shows nodes, latency, xruns, CPU usage

# Dump full graph as JSON
pw-dump                          # all objects
pw-dump <id>                     # specific object
pw-dump | jq '.[] | select(.type == "PipeWire:Interface:Node")'

# Monitor events
pw-mon                           # watch PipeWire events in real time
pw-cli dump                      # snapshot of current state

# Check for audio issues
pw-top                           # watch xrun column for glitches

@text
Recording and playback with PipeWire tools.

@code bash
# Record audio
pw-record output.wav                     # record default source
pw-record --target <id> output.wav       # record specific source
pw-record --format f32 --rate 48000 --channels 2 output.wav

# Play audio
pw-play input.wav
pw-play --target <id> input.wav          # play to specific sink

# MIDI
pw-midirecord output.mid
pw-midiplay input.mid

# Generate test signal
pw-cat --playback --format f32 --rate 48000 --channels 1 /dev/urandom

@text
PipeWire configuration on Artix Linux.

@code bash
# Config locations (copy from /usr/share/pipewire/ to override)
# ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf          # main config
# ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire-pulse.conf    # PulseAudio compat
# ~/.config/pipewire/client.conf            # client defaults

# WirePlumber config
# ~/.config/wireplumber/                    # WirePlumber overrides

# Set default sample rate
# In ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/99-custom.conf:
# context.properties = {
#     default.clock.rate = 48000
#     default.clock.allowed-rates = [ 44100 48000 96000 ]
# }

# Restart PipeWire after config changes
# Kill and let autostart restart it, or:
# killall pipewire pipewire-pulse wireplumber
# pipewire & pipewire-pulse & wireplumber &
